  "review": [
    "One typed Settings.TimeZone default is resolved before application resource acquisition; generated TOML/environment/typed overrides are exercised by an independent consumer.",
    "Clock validation is reused at the temporal owner; no dependency from temporal into database/application credential infrastructure was introduced.",
    "Calendar helpers delegate existing immutable temporal and scheduler policies. DST gaps/overlaps remain explicit, while calendar AddDays spans 23/25 elapsed hours when appropriate.",
    "Services and standard locations are snapshotted; concurrent applications and explicit overrides remain isolated without mutating time.Local.",
    "Log leaves inherit the application zone unless explicit. Both JSON timestamps and rollover use that zone. Archive filenames stay UTC; retention ages remain elapsed durations.",
    "Restart rollover derives the local date from file modification time. Existing size/count/age limits and file ownership guarantees remain covered by the logging race suite.",
    "Application report preparation passes the resolved Config into datatable.New; actual PostgreSQL CSV exports prove default and per-export timezone presentation. Configuration and export share one timezone length bound.",
    "Two compiler rejection fixtures preserve timezone/value types; three real gopls scenarios cover helpers, calendar declarations and generated override keys.",
    "All frozen runtime, generator, consumer, client and build inputs still match after verification; subsequent changes are documentation/evidence only."
  ],
